spans.s:
Haimavata,
(1) pl., n. of a school: Mvy 〔9092〕;
(2) n. of a yakṣa (= Pali Hema˚), regularly assoc. with Sātāgiri, q.v. (as in Pali with ˚gira): Mahāsamāj., Waldschmidt, Kl. Skt. Texte 4, 〔167.11〕 (pl.); Māy 〔87〕; 〔236.3〕 and 〔29〕 (Waldschmidt, ib. 〔175 n. 3〕); Samādh 〔p. 43 line 20〕; (listed with Sātāgiri among gandharvas) Suv 〔162.5〕; in Hoernle, MR 〔26.14〕 (Āṭānāṭiya Sūtra), corruptly Hīmavata.
